  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records establish that chemical SRO can be generated and varied using Monte Carlo or hybrid MD/MC simulations in refractory and other concentrated alloys, most directly in R1, and that SRO can form ordered nanoclusters, alter local lattice distortion, and create heterogeneous dislocation pathways. Thus they point toward computationally imposing SRO in a refractory HEA and examining a structure-sensitive property. However, none identifies HfTi/TiZr clustering in HfNbTaTiZr, B2-like percolating cluster networks, or the key thermal-transport mechanism in which reduced lattice-distortion scattering and conductive percolation outweigh precipitate scattering and modify high-frequency phonons. Reconstructing the specific conductivity-enhancement result would therefore require a substantial new mechanistic idea."
